1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:02,130
Thirteen rabbits got on a ship,

2
00:00:02,150 --> 00:00:03,520
family records say.

3
00:00:03,830 --> 00:00:05,640
Twenty-four got off.

4
00:00:05,890 --> 00:00:08,170
Turns out, rabbits can multiply.

5
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:11,400
Twenty-four became hundreds of millions.

6
00:00:11,770 --> 00:00:13,580
Australia fought back.

7
00:00:13,940 --> 00:00:14,960
Round one:

8
00:00:15,020 --> 00:00:16,060
a prize.

9
00:00:16,350 --> 00:00:18,080
Louis Pasteur entered.

10
00:00:18,210 --> 00:00:19,650
With chicken cholera.

11
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:23,380
The rules protected sheep, horses, dogs.

12
00:00:23,640 --> 00:00:24,990
They forgot birds.

13
00:00:25,260 --> 00:00:26,530
It didn't catch on.

14
00:00:26,710 --> 00:00:27,820
Nobody won.

15
00:00:28,210 --> 00:00:29,280
Round two:

16
00:00:29,340 --> 00:00:30,310
a fence.

17
00:00:30,460 --> 00:00:31,960
Ocean to ocean.

18
00:00:32,170 --> 00:00:33,550
Before it was finished,

19
00:00:33,570 --> 00:00:35,280
rabbits were on the safe side.

20
00:00:35,490 --> 00:00:37,530
Some scratched to get back out.

21
00:00:37,890 --> 00:00:39,010
Round three:

22
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:41,940
a rabbit virus, locked on an island.

23
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:44,810
It escaped, most likely on flies.

24
00:00:45,090 --> 00:00:45,605
Next year:

25
00:00:45,625 --> 00:00:47,890
an official release ceremony.

26
00:00:48,170 --> 00:00:50,250
The virus was already there.

27
00:00:50,490 --> 00:00:51,490
And it worked.

28
00:00:51,710 --> 00:00:52,940
Three rounds:

29
00:00:52,990 --> 00:00:54,170
Rabbits two.

30
00:00:54,190 --> 00:00:55,560
Flies one.

31
00:00:55,680 --> 00:00:57,460
Australia zero.

32
00:00:57,690 --> 00:00:58,520
They were winning before

33
00:00:58,540 --> 00:01:00,090
the ship even arrived.

34
00:01:00,420 --> 00:01:01,250
Probably.
